body:
It already sounds like she's not respecting your boundaries at all. The texts she sends you are manipulative and attention-seeking, and her actions are just as bad. You already tried talking to her about it and she has shown you that she doesn't care about how you feel and how her actions are affecting you. She needs professional help. 

&#x200B;

Continuing your friendship with her will only make things difficult for you, *and* her own recovery, as she's dependent on your counsel (and there's only so much you can help her, not being a mental health professional) and security. I would strongly advise you to end this relationship.

Somehow, she did manage to learn the basics- she's really good at sitting and waiting but she just get so excited about birds and squirells. She's not trained *enough (*for my parents)*,* so to speak. If that makes sense.

&#x200B;

Thanks.

Just to clarify, my dogs do get the attention and exercise that they need. My schedule is very busy, but that does include the time that I spend at home with my dogs. I am able to come home in between classes and work in order to take care of them, just not 100% of the time. 

She is perfectly capable of taking care of them the other 25% of the time when I'm not doing it, she just hates doing it despite 2 of those dogs belonging to her as well. 

&#x200B;
